    sections: [{"h2": "What makes a bank 'good' for expats", "paras": ["For expats, the best bank account is the one that accepts your residency, works in the currencies you use, and does not charge you for every international move. A high-street bank that is perfect at home can become expensive or even close your account once you move."]}, {"h2": "Your four main options", "paras": ["Most expats combine two or three of these."], "list": ["A local bank account in your new country for salary, rent and bills", "Your home-country account, if the bank still serves non-residents", "A multi-currency account (such as Wise or Revolut) for transfers and spending", "An international or offshore expat bank for higher balances and wealth services"]}, {"h2": "Fees that quietly add up", "paras": ["Watch for foreign transaction fees on cards, poor exchange rates on transfers, international wire fees, monthly account fees and minimum balance requirements. A multi-currency account often removes most of these for day-to-day use."]}, {"h2": "International expat banks", "paras": ["Several large banks run international or offshore divisions aimed at expats. They can offer accounts in multiple currencies and relationship managers, but often require high minimum balances or income. They suit higher earners who move often; most people do not need one."]}, {"h2": "Opening an account before you move", "paras": ["Some banks and fintech apps let you open an account before you arrive, which helps with your first rent payment and salary. Others require a local address and residence permit. See our guide on how to open a bank account abroad for the documents to prepare."]}, {"h2": "A simple setup that works for most expats", "paras": ["Keep one home account for any income and obligations back home, open a local account once you have residency, and use a multi-currency account to move money between them at a fair rate. Review fees once a year as your situation changes."]}],
    title: "Best Bank Accounts for Expats 2026: Zero-Fee, Global Access, Actually Work Abroad",
    excerpt: "Local banks, home accounts, multi-currency apps and international expat banks: how to pick the right mix for life abroad and avoid hidden fees.",
    category: "banking",
    tags: ["expat bank account", "Charles Schwab", "N26", "Monzo", "zero foreign transaction fees"],
