    sections: [{"h2": "What SafetyWing Nomad Insurance is", "paras": ["SafetyWing Nomad Insurance is travel medical insurance designed for digital nomads and long-term travellers. It works like a subscription: you can pay monthly and keep it running while you travel, rather than buying a fixed trip policy."]}, {"h2": "What it typically covers", "paras": ["Coverage centres on unexpected medical events and emergencies abroad. Exact benefits depend on the plan and your policy wording, so read the current terms before you buy."], "list": ["Emergency medical treatment and hospital stays", "Emergency evacuation", "Some travel disruptions, depending on plan", "Limited coverage in your home country under specific conditions", "Optional add-ons, such as adventure sports, depending on availability"]}, {"h2": "Important limits to check", "paras": ["Like most travel medical insurance, it is not full health insurance. Pre-existing conditions, routine check-ups and many planned treatments are typically excluded or limited. Check deductibles, maximum limits, age-related pricing, and how coverage works if you visit your home country or the US."]}, {"h2": "Who it suits", "paras": ["It suits younger, healthy nomads who move between countries and want flexible, affordable emergency coverage. It suits less well people who need ongoing care, are settling long term in one country, or need coverage that local residency or visa rules require."]}, {"h2": "Alternatives to compare", "paras": ["If you need more comprehensive cover, look at international private medical insurance from providers focused on expats, or local health insurance once you have residency. Some visas require specific minimum coverage, so check your visa conditions first."]}, {"h2": "Before you buy", "paras": ["Compare at least two quotes, read the policy wording rather than the marketing page, and check the claims process. Keep receipts and medical reports during any treatment so claims go smoothly."]}],
