    faq: [{"q": "Can I use travel insurance for a year abroad?", "a": "Some policies allow long durations, but many limit trip length or exclude routine care. Read the maximum trip length and the definition of residence."}, {"q": "What is the main difference?", "a": "Travel insurance focuses on unexpected events during a trip. Expat insurance is designed to support ongoing healthcare while living abroad."}, {"q": "Do visas ask for a specific type of insurance?", "a": "Some visas require proof of insurance meeting stated conditions. Check the official requirements."}, {"q": "What about nomad-style insurance?", "a": "Some products aim at remote workers who travel, combining features of both. Check coverage details, exclusions and where you are covered."}, {"q": "Does either cover my home country?", "a": "Often home-country visits are limited or excluded. Check the policy."}],
